  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SP&amp;LR for Asia WWs-Agri-food System</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Marginalized workers in Southeat Asia and South Asia, especially women workers in agri-food sector, are able to voice up  their demands for transformative social protection and enjoy more inclusive, just and comprehensive social protection.

Grassrootsorganizations of marginalized workers, especially women workers groups in agri-food sector in SEA and SA, are empowered with advocacy capacity to defend their demands for transformative social protection through networking at sub regional and regional levels.

1)- Democraticorganizations of marginalized workers, especially women workers in agri-food sector in SEA and SA, have improved knowledge and awareness on risks, challenges and vulnerabilities that women in the agri-food sector face and their needof social protection,

2)- Democratic organizations of marginalized workers, especially women workers in agri-food sector in SEA and SA, have increased capacity inhaving common ambition, agenda and demands for transformative gender social protection through networking and allying with each other and with other like-minded organizations and individuals at sub regional and regional levels;

3)- Women and Children Committee of ASEAN put maternity protection for agri-food sector workers on its agenda.</narrative>
  </description>
